Purpose of this document
------------------------
This document has notes about the project's support for iOS/iPadOS devices. The
oldest iOS/iPadOS version still supported is defined by
IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET (search keyword: deployment target). The source for
the information which iOS versions support which devices is Wikipedia.
- https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_iPhone_models
- https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_iPad_models
- https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPod

The source for logical and pixel screen resolutions is iOS Ref. For devices not
listed on that site, the pixel resolution is taken from Wikipedia.
- https://iosref.com/res

iOS / device support
--------------------
The devices listed under each iOS version are the ones for which that iOS
version is the last one to support the device. If the project stops supporting
a given iOS version then all devices listed under that iOS version, and older
iOS versions, will no longer be able to run the app.

Each iPhone and iPad device list entry also shows the screen resolutions of the
listed device(s). The format is "logical/point resolution (pixel resolution)".
The screen resolution is interesting so that when changes are made to the UI,
these changes can be tested on the devices with the most space-constrained
screens. Currently those devices are:
- iPhone SE 2nd / 3rd generation / iPhone 8 (375 × 667)
- iPad Mini 5th generation / iPad 5th / 6th generation / iPad Pro 9.7 inch (768 × 1024)
  iPad Mini 6th / 7th generation are slightly less wide, but higher (744 × 1133)

